  "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nThis updates the signature of the `createURL` function given to widgets' lifecycle (`init` and `render`). It also updates the undocumented top-level `createURL` to match the same signature.\r\n\r\n## New signature\r\n\r\nThe signature at the widget level (given to the `init` and `render` hooks) stays the same:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ncreateURL(nextState: SearchParameters): string;\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, the internal signature in the `index` widget changes and uses the UI state.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ncreateURL(nextState: UIState): string;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis UI state is accumulated with all the widgets mounted on the instance, which results in the complete UI state of the sub indices.\r\n\r\nThis change is especially needed for generating exhaustive URLs for both `currentRefinement` and `clearRefinements`.\r\n\r\n## Current architecture limitations\r\n\r\nThe new architecture for v4 proceeds top to bottom. This means that if you call `createURL` in a top-level widget `init` hook, it ignores the `uiState` of all children. This results in an incomplete URL string.\r\n\r\nThis likely will never happen in user code because we rarely only use `init` without `render`. Still, if we've got complains about incomplete URLs, we can suggest adding a `render` method to fix the issue.\r\n\r\n## Notes on top-level `createURL`\r\n\r\nThe top-level `createURL` method has never been documented and was initially introduced for our Magento integration. This is not used anymore so we might consider removing this method by the time we go stable.\r\n\r\nSee #372 and #377.\r\n\r\n## What's remaining\r\n\r\nThere are some checks that we need to proceed and to fix in others PRs if the result is not expected.\r\n\r\n- Check the `createURL` usage in `currentRefinements`\r\n- Check the `createURL` usage in `clearRefinements`",
